#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0616 expect=violation domain=ADSL
#note "trcmpg1 / trcmpg1n spelled in lower case. Column names match case-insensitively on every surface (owner ruling 2026-09-28), so the lowercase spelling a SAS dataset may carry satisfies the Requirements.Variables.All templates and the rule executes with the same verdict as on the uppercase twin (PMDA-AD0616-invalid_minority_row): one expansion (y=1); group TRCMPG1N=1 holds {HIGH x2, LOW x1} -> one minority row (PMDA-AD0616: TRCMPGy must hold one value per TRCMPGyN)."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=3 USUBJID=003
dataset ADSL
col STUDYID   type=Char
col USUBJID   type=Char
col trcmpg1   type=Char
col trcmpg1n  type=Num
---
S1 | 001 | HIGH | 1
S1 | 002 | HIGH | 1
S1 | 003 | LOW  | 1
---
